// ── ziggfreed-common's type scale: every text size the family draws ───────────
// Imported per document as:  $ZT = "../Common/ZigType.ui";  (from Pages/; "ZigType.ui" from Common/) and used as
//   Style: (FontSize: $ZT.@ZigFontBody, TextColor: ...);
// so a size changes here, once, for every page, HUD and toast of zc and the mods built on it. The client's own
// HUD reads a shared size the same way (Interface/InGame/Hud/ObjectivePanelObjectiveSlot.ui:
// FontSize: $ObjectiveCommon.@FontSize). com.ziggfreed.common.ui.ZigType holds the same numbers for the few sizes
// Java sets, and ZigTypeTest holds the two together.
//
// The rule: no player text under 13; descriptions, captions and hints 13;
// row labels and body text 14; headings and titles keep their sizes. A document never writes a size under
// @ZigFontEmphasis as a number (the family's RepoHygieneTest), and MinShrinkTextToFitFontSize takes these steps
// too, so shrink-to-fit never draws under the floor.

// The floor: captions, descriptions, hints, counts, timestamps, a row's second line.
@ZigFontCaption = 13;
// An uppercase section label (vanilla's own section label is 13, bold, uppercase).
@ZigFontSection = 13;
// Row labels, body text, buttons, fields, chips.
@ZigFontBody = 14;
// A name that leads its row or card.
@ZigFontEmphasis = 15;
// A heading inside a page.
@ZigFontHeading = 16;
// A large heading or a sub-title.
@ZigFontSubtitle = 18;
// A page title.
@ZigFontTitle = 20;
// A big number.
@ZigFontDisplay = 22;
@ZigFontDisplayLarge = 24;
// A hero title over full-width art (the Almanac's season name), the largest step.
@ZigFontHero = 28;

// The ONE exception under the floor: a label inside a
// HUD box too small for 13 (a HUD bar's end words, an ability cooldown's key, the mob inspector's HP text).
// The family's RepoHygieneTest allows it in those documents only.
@ZigFontMicro = 11;
